# Walter monitoring stack (`/srv/monitoring`)

Prometheus, Grafana, node-exporter, cAdvisor, dcgm-exporter, blackbox_exporter, and a small llama-swap discovery sidecar.
Everything runs with `network_mode: host` and **listens on 127.0.0.1 only**. Nothing is published on ${BACKEND_WG_IP}, the LAN, or 0.0.0.0,
and no UFW or DOCKER-USER rule was added.

## Access (SSH tunnel from the workstation)

```bash
ssh -N -L 3001:127.0.0.1:3001 -L 9090:127.0.0.1:9090 ${BACKEND_SSH_USER}@${BACKEND_LAN_IP}
```

- Grafana: http://localhost:3001. User `admin`; the password is in `/srv/monitoring/grafana-admin-password` (root 600): `sudo cat /srv/monitoring/grafana-admin-password`
- Prometheus: http://localhost:9090 (targets: `/targets`, alerts: `/alerts`). It has no auth, so it is reachable only through the tunnel.

Dashboards (folder **Spark**):
| Dashboard | UID | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Spark overview (home) | `spark-overview` | built here: `grafana/build_spark_overview.py` |
| Node Exporter Full | `rYdddlPWk` | grafana.com ID 1860 rev 45, JSON committed |
| NVIDIA DCGM Exporter Dashboard | `Oxed_c6Wz` | grafana.com ID 12239 rev 2, JSON committed |

Alerts: `prometheus/rules/spark-alerts.yml`. There is no Alertmanager. Firing alerts show in Prometheus `/alerts` and in Grafana
(Alerting → Alert rules, data source-managed "Prometheus").

## Layout

```
compose.yaml                         all services, images pinned by digest
prometheus/prometheus.yml            scrape config        prometheus/rules/*.yml  alert rules
blackbox/blackbox.yml                probe modules (http_2xx, http_401)
llamaswap-sd/llamaswap_sd.py         polls llama-swap /running + /v1/models every 15 s
grafana/provisioning/                datasource + dashboards (json/)
grafana/build_spark_overview.py      generator for spark-overview.json (edit + re-run; Grafana reloads in 60 s)
grafana-admin-password               root 600 (canonical)
secrets/  (root 700)                 container copies: grafana-admin-password (uid 472, 0400),
                                     llama-swap-api-key (uid 65534, 0400)
```

Named volumes: `monitoring_prometheus-data` (30 d retention), `monitoring_grafana-data`, `monitoring_llamaswap-sd`.

